sentences.text:
Accordingly, anticipatory bail application stands allowed with a direction that in the event of arrest of the applicant, he shall be released on Anticipatory Bail on his furnishing a personal bond and two sureties, each in the like amount, to the satisfaction of Court concerned, and even if the applicant is not arrested, he shall appear before the Trial Court within a period of two weeks from today and he shall be released on bail in the aforesaid case crime on his furnishing a personal bond and two sureties, each in the like amount, to the satisfaction of Court concerned on the following conditions and subject to any other conditions that may be fixed by the Trial Court:
(i) That the applicant shall file an application for his D.N.A. test and the trial Court shall take a suitable decision on the aforesaid application in accordance with law.
(ii). That the applicant shall appear before the trial court on each date fixed, unless his personal presence is exempted;
(iii). That the applicant shall not, directly or indirectly make any inducement, threat or promise to any person acquainted with the facts of the case so as to dissuade him from disclosing such facts to the court or to any police officer or tamper with the evidence;

